  "notes": "{漕|こ}ぐ is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) used for rowing boats or pedaling bicycles/swings.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{漕|こ}いでいる indicates rowing or pedaling is ongoing.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [boat]を{漕|こ}ぐ — to row [boat]\n- [bicycle]を{漕|こ}ぐ — to pedal [bicycle]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {舟|ふね}を{漕|こ}ぐ (row a boat)\n- {自転車|じてんしゃ}を{漕|こ}ぐ (pedal a bicycle)\n- ブランコを{漕|こ}ぐ (swing on a swing)\n- オールを{漕|こ}ぐ (row with oars)\n\nIDIOMATIC:\n{船|ふね}を{漕|こ}ぐ when describing someone's head nodding while dozing (head moves like rowing motion).\n\nOFTEN IN HIRAGANA:\nThis verb is frequently written as こぐ.",
